    "cards": [
        {
            "dot": "emerald",
            "title": "Nothing imports a handler",
            "items": [
                "A cross-handler dependency goes through the proxy, which is what keeps inversion of control intact",
                "The same indirection lets a mock handler replace an adapter for one test",
                "And lets a changed file be swapped without restarting the process"
            ]
        },
        {
            "dot": "cyan",
            "title": "The type is the contract",
            "items": [
                "Exporting a Handler type is what makes the framework generate the schema and validate the call",
                "The same type produces the API documentation, so the two cannot disagree",
                "Configuration schemas sit beside the component they configure"
            ]
        },
        {
            "dot": "amber",
            "title": "Free once the call is described",
            "items": [
                "A checkpoint records the step and the branch a run took; the semantic log turns those into observed flows",
                "Caching, dependency analysis and coverage attribution read the same method registry",
                "None of this is code the handler author writes"
            ]
        }
    ]
